<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-04--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch15-04: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.43";
    dc:description "The mechanism makes measurable temporal predictions, but the decisive physiological variables are absent from standard repositories. Existing morphology cannot distinguish peristaltic pressure from other developmental causes.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Synchronize in vivo oviduct pressure maps and peristaltic-wave direction with repeated imaging of the deformable egg, then test whether peak pressure lies posterior to mid-egg and predicts anterior broadening, posterior taper and blunt-end-first transport. Mismatched pressure location or transport orientation would refute the mechanism.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Direct oviduct imaging and manometry are specialized and invasive.", "Final shape alone cannot localize the causal pressure maximum.", "Public egg-shape datasets do not include spatial pressure during shell formation.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.78"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.427"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
